    "reason": "The bay opening and clip-relief spans (14.1-15.6 mm) and the gate-slot cap print across air; the slow local speeds give each span time to set. Cooling is not part of the local recipe: fan is a filament-profile setting (fan_min_speed 40 %, fan_cooling_layer_time 30 s), so in these long layers the base fan falls to 40 % and only paths the slicer classifies as overhang wall or bridge get the 90 % overhang/bridge fan; gap-fill and inner-wall paths in the bands print at 40 %. Actual F, M106 and per-feature path lengths by fan level are read back from the G-code into slice-clearances.json; digital evidence does not predict PETG droop, inspect and trim the roofs."
